WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.896 --> 00:00:14.640
There hadn't been a celebration at Dorincourt Castle for years.

2
00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:21.181
But now the earl wanted to throw a grand dinner party to show off his grandson.

3
00:00:22.362 --> 00:00:25.703
He had no idea that bad news would arrive that night.

4
00:00:27.283 --> 00:00:30.384
The earl invited all the lords and ladies he knew.

5
00:00:32.692 --> 00:00:35.294
He even invited his sister, Constantia, to visit.

6
00:00:36.575 --> 00:00:40.959
They'd quarreled 35 years ago, and he hadn't seen her since.

7
00:00:44.021 --> 00:00:46.603
Constantia arrived a few days before the party.

8
00:00:48.585 --> 00:00:51.047
The first thing she wanted was to meet Cedric.

9
00:00:51.948 --> 00:00:56.852
"I've heard the boy has worked miracles on you, John," she teased her brother.

10
00:00:58.064 --> 00:01:02.888
"Some of the tenants have even stopped calling you 'the wicked Earl of Dorincourt.'"

11
00:01:04.149 --> 00:01:05.350
The earl scowled.

12
00:01:05.370 --> 00:01:08.172
"I don't know about that."

13
00:01:09.574 --> 00:01:12.456
His face brightened when Cedric entered the library.

14
00:01:12.476 --> 00:01:16.059
"Come here, Cedric!"

15
00:01:17.980 --> 00:01:22.664
The boy ran to his grandfather, who held out a hand to a lady with white curls and

16
00:01:22.744 --> 00:01:23.685
friendly eyes.

17
00:01:23.705 --> 00:01:29.001
"I'd like you to meet your great-aunt, Lady Constantia."

18
00:01:31.163 --> 00:01:32.323
Cedric shook her hand.

19
00:01:32.343 --> 00:01:36.346
"I'm pleased to meet you, Great-Aunt Constantia."

20
00:01:37.387 --> 00:01:39.428
Constantia smiled warmly at him.

21
00:01:39.448 --> 00:01:44.972
"I was always fond of your papa, and you remind me so much of him."

22
00:01:44.992 --> 00:01:51.396
"It makes me happy when people say that, because everyone liked him," Cedric said.

23
00:01:51.416 --> 00:01:54.058
"Everyone likes my mother too.

24
00:01:55.278 --> 00:01:57.240
While you're here, I hope you can meet her."

25
00:01:58.672 --> 00:01:59.993
"I hope so too."

26
00:02:01.193 --> 00:02:04.354
Constantia raised her eyebrows at the earl, who looked away.

27
00:02:04.375 --> 00:02:10.517
"The workmen are putting a new roof on a cottage," Cedric said to his grandfather.

28
00:02:10.537 --> 00:02:12.938
"Do you want to ride over to watch?"

29
00:02:14.459 --> 00:02:16.880
"Another time," the earl said.

30
00:02:16.900 --> 00:02:20.321
"Wilkins will take you riding today."

31
00:02:22.742 --> 00:02:27.184
After Cedric left the library, the earl and his sister sat down for tea.

32
00:02:28.476 --> 00:02:31.278
"You couldn't have found a better heir."

33
00:02:35.660 --> 00:02:37.161
Constantia poured the tea.

34
00:02:37.181 --> 00:02:40.983
"You must be pleased."

35
00:02:41.003 --> 00:02:45.606
"He's a fine fellow, and we're great friends."

36
00:02:46.687 --> 00:02:48.288
The earl started to smile.

37
00:02:48.308 --> 00:02:51.690
"I've actually become quite fond of him."

38
00:02:51.710 --> 00:02:55.212
"What does his mother think of you?"

39
00:02:57.396 --> 00:02:59.897
The earl's smile faded into another scowl.

40
00:03:00.897 --> 00:03:02.397
"I haven't asked her."

41
00:03:02.417 --> 00:03:07.939
"I must be frank with you, John, and say that I don't approve of what you've done.

42
00:03:08.999 --> 00:03:11.380
It's wrong to separate the child from his mother."

43
00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:14.201
Constantia put down her teacup.

44
00:03:15.361 --> 00:03:17.041
"I intend to call on her tomorrow.

45
00:03:17.982 --> 00:03:20.802
So if you're going to quarrel with me, you'd better do it now."

46
00:03:22.223 --> 00:03:25.884
The earl had forgotten that his sister never hesitated to say what she thought.

47
00:03:27.648 --> 00:03:34.210
"From what I've heard," Constantia said, "she has been a wonderful influence on her son.

48
00:03:35.451 --> 00:03:38.532
I've also heard that your tenants adore her."

49
00:03:38.552 --> 00:03:41.873
"They adore him."

50
00:03:42.573 --> 00:03:44.234
The earl corrected his sister.

51
00:03:44.254 --> 00:03:47.315
"You can go see her, if you like.

52
00:03:48.515 --> 00:03:50.816
Just don't try to make me visit her!"

53
00:03:55.808 --> 00:03:58.410
The next day Constantia returned from visiting Mrs.

54
00:03:58.530 --> 00:04:05.054
Errol. "She's a perfectly lovely person," Constantia told her brother.

55
00:04:05.074 --> 00:04:09.517
"You should thank her for making Cedric the fine boy that he is."

56
00:04:10.918 --> 00:04:12.760
The earl harrumphed at Constantia.

57
00:04:13.880 --> 00:04:16.382
But she noticed he didn't say anything bad about Mrs.

58
00:04:16.462 --> 00:04:20.885
Errol. The dinner party was that night.

59
00:04:22.226 --> 00:04:24.788
Cedric put on his best black velvet suit.

60
00:04:26.208 --> 00:04:30.612
Before he went downstairs to the ballroom, he stuffed Dick's handkerchief into a pocket.

61
00:04:30.632 --> 00:04:36.938
"I wish Dick could see me wearing this to a party," he said to himself.

62
00:04:39.521 --> 00:04:42.123
At the party all the guests wanted to talk to Cedric.

63
00:04:43.785 --> 00:04:46.808
They smiled when he showed them Dick's red-and-purple gift.

64
00:04:48.449 --> 00:04:50.852
They were charmed by his kindness toward the earl.

65
00:04:53.132 --> 00:04:56.974
Constantia watched as Cedric followed his grandfather around the ballroom.

66
00:04:56.994 --> 00:05:02.696
"John's own sons never paid him this much attention," she thought.

67
00:05:03.756 --> 00:05:06.257
"No wonder John enjoys his company."

68
00:05:07.878 --> 00:05:09.719
Soon a footman approached the earl.

69
00:05:09.739 --> 00:05:12.740
"Should I announce that dinner is served, my lord?"

70
00:05:14.761 --> 00:05:16.682
The earl looked at his watch and frowned.

71
00:05:16.702 --> 00:05:19.143
"Mr. Havisham isn't here yet.

72
00:05:20.343 --> 00:05:21.904
Has there been any word from him?"

73
00:05:23.364 --> 00:05:24.004
"No, my lord."

74
00:05:24.024 --> 00:05:27.306
"This is most unusual.

75
00:05:28.426 --> 00:05:30.687
Mr. Havisham is always on time."

76
00:05:31.788 --> 00:05:33.588
The earl checked his watch again.

77
00:05:33.608 --> 00:05:37.450
"We'll wait a few more minutes.

78
00:05:39.211 --> 00:05:41.491
Let me know the moment his carriage arrives."

79
00:05:43.312 --> 00:05:46.534
The footman turned and spotted the tall lawyer entering the room.

80
00:05:46.554 --> 00:05:49.675
"Mr. Havisham has arrived, my lord."

81
00:05:50.535 --> 00:05:54.073
"Yes, I can see that," the earl said impatiently.

82
00:05:54.093 --> 00:05:56.514
"Good evening, Mr.

83
00:05:56.975 --> 00:05:58.416
Cedric started to call out.

84
00:05:58.436 --> 00:06:01.057
"Havisham, where have you been?

85
00:06:02.118 --> 00:06:02.918
Why are you late?"

86
00:06:03.199 --> 00:06:04.299
the earl demanded.

87
00:06:04.319 --> 00:06:06.240
"What's wrong?"

88
00:06:08.022 --> 00:06:12.564
Mr. Havisham, who was never agitated, was pale and obviously upset.

89
00:06:13.965 --> 00:06:18.048
Before the lawyer could reply, a second footman arrived at the earl's side.

90
00:06:19.296 --> 00:06:22.597
"Cook says dinner will be ruined if it's not served immediately."

91
00:06:22.617 --> 00:06:25.778
"Then announce that dinner is served!"

92
00:06:26.158 --> 00:06:27.279
the earl snarled.

93
00:06:27.299 --> 00:06:32.001
"Havisham! Tell me what's wrong at once!"

94
00:06:33.581 --> 00:06:36.602
Mr. Havisham glanced around uneasily at the guests.

95
00:06:36.622 --> 00:06:38.963
"Not here.

96
00:06:39.443 --> 00:06:41.724
You'll want to hear the news in private."
